    "title": "Head volleyball coach dismissed from Texas Tech amid abuse claims - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Urijah Jaushlin ,\n1 days ago\nLUBBOCK, Texas -- New details have emerged about the dismissal of former Texas Tech volleyball coach Tony Graystone , which involve allegations of abuse and a felony battery incident, according to an open records request obtained on Wednesday.\nAn open records request revealed that on September 7, 2026, Kirby Hocutt, Texas Tech's athletics director, received a complaint. The complaint expressed a desire to meet with Hocutt to discuss allegations of physical abuse, medical mistreatment and felony battery committed by Graystone.\nCody Campbell reacts to Protect College Sports Act passing Senate The reporting party asked Hocutt not to talk to Coach Graystone before the meeting, \"Due to fear of increased retaliation and intimidation by Coach Graystone,\" the email stated.\nOn September 13, Hocutt issued a letter to Graystone, stating in part, \"Texas Tech is exercising its right under Section 5.A. of your Employment Contract to terminate your employment for cause effective immediately.\"\nEverythingLubbock previously reported that Associate head coach Alisa Blair was promoted to interim head coach for the remainder of the season for Texas Tech.\nGraystone served as the head coach of the Red Raiders for the past ten seasons and was in the middle of his eleventh year in Lubbock.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KLBK | KAMC | EverythingLubbock.com.\n1",
    "summary": "An open records request revealed that on September 7, 2026, Kirby Hocutt, Texas Tech's athletics director, received a complaint. The complaint expressed a desire to meet with Hocutt to discuss allegations of physical abuse, medical mistreatment and felony battery committed by Graystone. Cody Campbell reacts to Protect College Sports Act passing Senate The reporting party asked Hocutt not to talk to Coach Graystone before the meeting, \"Due to fear of increased retaliation and intimidation by Coach Graystone,\" the email stated.",
